Let's create another feature to our project - Conversation Memory. The Conversation memory is storing individual Conversation History items in a more efficient way, essentially, it gets the Conversation History item and summarizes the message in a meaningfull way. So for each Conversation History item exist one Conversation memory item, simply representing summary of the conversation history item.

The actual create step for conversation memory happens usually once a day is considered a background process. For our project we will add a user-requested creation of conversation memory: on each Conversation History item displayed in frontend will be a button (similar to current rename and delete) which will kick off the background API for creation of conversation memory.

The backend should contain conversation memory APIS - creation, list, delete - basic CRUD. The creation should be done by simple custom agent (agent framework) with a summarization prompt and vectorization step (embedding model). The conversation memory is stored in pgsql (running locally in docker - see #pgsql folder with pgvector extension).

The backend should also implement API which will do vector search over the database based on input text. The search returns top 10 rows.

Create a carefull design for this feature only, no code yet.